-- title:
--   Exact logarithmic growth rate of the rounded band count
-- statement:
--   Let $g(n)$ be the executable band size: the ceiling of the square root of the typed output count, divided by $2^{\mu(n)/20}$ using ceiling division. Define $b(n)=\lceil n/g(n)\rceil$. Write $H_2(x)=-x\log_2x-(1-x)\log_2(1-x)$, $E=128H_2(1/256)$, and $\delta=-1/20$. Then
--   $$
--   \lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{\log b(n)}{\log n}
--   =1-\frac{E+\delta}{5}.
--   $$
--   This identifies the exponent of the actual integer band count, including both rounding operations used by the construction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/HierarchyScales.lean#L311-L330

